# model.pkl is intentionally NOT ignored here (Phase 2 change).
#
# It was DVC-cached-only in Phase 1, which meant it lived only in whoever's
# local .dvc/cache ran `dvc repro` -- no DVC remote is configured (see
# .dvc/config), so a fresh clone (CI runner, Render, a teammate's machine)
# had no way to obtain it. Since Docker/CI/Render all build straight from
# the git clone, we changed dvc.yaml's train stage to `cache: false` for
# this output (same pattern already used for metrics.json) so model.pkl is
# tracked directly in git instead. dvc.lock still pins its hash for
# reproducibility checks. See docs/deployment.md for the full rationale
# and the "proper" alternative (a real DVC remote) if this project grows
# past a course deployment.
